WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.757
Query, Key, and Value become much easier once we give each one a job.

00:00:04.757 --> 00:00:08.502
The Query represents what the current token is looking for.

00:00:08.502 --> 00:00:13.552
The Key represents how each available token can be matched against that request.

00:00:13.552 --> 00:00:19.207
The Value contains the information that can be passed forward when a token is considered useful.

00:00:19.207 --> 00:00:22.957
Every token can produce all three representations.

00:00:22.957 --> 00:00:27.787
The model compares a Query with many Keys to create compatibility scores.

00:00:27.787 --> 00:00:31.347
Softmax turns those scores into attention weights.

00:00:31.347 --> 00:00:36.132
The weights then determine how strongly the corresponding Values are blended together.

00:00:36.132 --> 00:00:39.327
A useful analogy is information retrieval.

00:00:39.327 --> 00:00:46.362
A query expresses a need, keys help identify relevant items, and values provide the content.

00:00:46.362 --> 00:00:52.112
The analogy is not mathematically exact, but it gives us a practical mental model before we look at

00:00:52.112 --> 00:00:53.518
the matrix operations.
